import GroupApproximation.Analysis.UniversalCStarAmalgam

/-!
# Shulman's symmetric amalgam theorem, as the notes cite it

`non_mf_group_notes.tex`, proof of the exact-radical computation:

> Shulman's symmetric amalgam theorem [Sh, Theorem 10] makes the full unital
> amalgam `A *_C A` MF.

`shulman_symmetricAmalgam_isMFAlgebra` below is that sentence, at the
repository's own full amalgam.

## Which input is cited, and why

Exactly one: **Shulman, Theorem 10** — for a separable MF `C*`-algebra `A` and
a unital `C*`-subalgebra `C ⊆ A`, the full unital amalgamated free product
`A *_C A` is MF.  That is the single `sorry` of this file.

The *object* is not cited.  The note that graded this sentence `partial` in
`metadata/NON_MF_SENTENCE_MAP.tsv` records two missing pieces — the full
`C*`-amalgamated free product, and Theorem 10 — and the first of them is no
longer missing.  `Analysis/UniversalCStarAmalgam.lean` constructs the full
amalgam from first principles, as the closed `*`-subalgebra generated by the
two diagonal factor maps inside the bounded product of all same-universe
compatible pairs of representations, and proves its universal property
(`universalCStarAmalgam_existsUnique_lift`): every pair of `*`-homomorphisms out
of the two factors that agree on `C` factors uniquely through it.  So the
amalgam `A *_C A` of the printed sentence is a defined object of the
repository, `UniversalCStarAmalgam i i` for the inclusion `i : C →⋆ₐ[ℂ] A`, and
only the MF conclusion about it is taken from the literature.

The instance hypothesis `[Nonempty (CStarAmalgamRepresentation i i)]` is the
repository's standing side condition on that construction — the ambient product
is indexed by compatible representations, so one is needed for the object to be
formed.  It is not an extra mathematical assumption of Shulman's theorem; it is
how `Analysis/UniversalCStarAmalgam.lean` states every result about the amalgam.

## The symmetric form is the one that is cited

Theorem 10 is about `A *_C A`: two copies of one separable MF algebra over one
subalgebra.  The general amalgam `A *_C B` is a strictly larger theorem and is
not stated here, because the notes do not use it — `Sofic/SymmetricDoubleCovering.lean`
records that the `C₂` free-lamp amalgam of the argument needs only the
symmetric form.

## What is proved rather than cited

The heredity step the notes take immediately afterwards — *"Subgroups of MF
groups are MF"* at the algebra level.  `isMFAlgebra_of_injective_into_symmetricAmalgam`
derives it from `IsMFAlgebra.of_injective_nonUnitalStarAlgHom`, which is
unconditional in `Analysis/MFAlgebra.lean`: bare corona embeddability composes
with any injective nonunital `*`-homomorphism, and separability of the source
follows because an injective `*`-homomorphism of `C*`-algebras is isometric.

This sentence is not used in `non_mf_groups_exist.tex`; it belongs to the notes.
-/

namespace GroupApproximation
namespace Manuscript
namespace NonMF
namespace PriorWork

universe u v

-- LITERATURE INPUT (sorry): Shulman, The MF property for amalgamated free
-- products, arXiv:2603.13564 (v2, 22 March 2026), Theorem 10.
/-- **Shulman, Theorem 10, the symmetric amalgam theorem.**

> Shulman's symmetric amalgam theorem [Sh, Theorem 10] makes the full unital
> amalgam `A *_C A` MF.

For a separable MF `C*`-algebra `A` and a unital `C*`-subalgebra `C ⊆ A`,
presented as an injective unital `*`-homomorphism `i : C →⋆ₐ[ℂ] A`, the full
unital amalgamated free product of two copies of `A` over `C` is MF.

Separability of `A` is carried inside `IsMFAlgebra A`.  The amalgam is the
repository's own `UniversalCStarAmalgam i i`, with its universal property
proved in `Analysis/UniversalCStarAmalgam.lean`; only the MF conclusion is
cited. -/
theorem shulman_symmetricAmalgam_isMFAlgebra
    {C A : Type u} [CStarAlgebra C] [CStarAlgebra A]
    (i : C →⋆ₐ[ℂ] A) (_hi : Function.Injective i) (_hA : IsMFAlgebra A)
    [Nonempty (CStarAmalgamRepresentation i i)] :
    IsMFAlgebra (UniversalCStarAmalgam i i) :=
  sorry

/-- **The heredity step the notes take next**, at the algebra level:

> Subgroups of MF groups are MF.

Any `C*`-algebra admitting an injective, possibly nonunital, `*`-homomorphism
into the symmetric amalgam `A *_C A` is itself MF.  The amalgam is MF by the
cited Theorem 10; the passage to the subalgebra is
`IsMFAlgebra.of_injective_nonUnitalStarAlgHom`, which is unconditional. -/
theorem isMFAlgebra_of_injective_into_symmetricAmalgam
    {C A : Type u} {B : Type v} [CStarAlgebra C] [CStarAlgebra A]
    [NonUnitalCStarAlgebra B]
    (i : C →⋆ₐ[ℂ] A) (hi : Function.Injective i) (hA : IsMFAlgebra A)
    [Nonempty (CStarAmalgamRepresentation i i)]
    (j : B →⋆ₙₐ[ℂ] UniversalCStarAmalgam i i) (hj : Function.Injective j) :
    IsMFAlgebra B :=
  (shulman_symmetricAmalgam_isMFAlgebra i hi hA).of_injective_nonUnitalStarAlgHom
    j hj

end PriorWork
end NonMF
end Manuscript
end GroupApproximation
